--- body ---
## Context

Goal 1 of the ladder (`README.md`): *nothing leaves this machine unasked, one
obvious switch stops the work, and uninstall removes every declared piece of
derived state and leaves no undeclared residue.* Three terms since 2026-09-03,
when R31 was retired: **R10, R15, R22**. It is the lowest rung because its
assertions need no corpus, no build and no library.

This tracker holds one question: **is goal 1 kept for zoteus?** Today it is not,
and the reasons are below. The assertions all exist — seven checks in
`bench/acceptance/assertions.py`, each with a fail-control — so what is missing
is the target's side, not the instrument's.

## Where the rung stands for zoteus

From `bench/results/0604-ladder-matrix/MATRIX.md`, run 2026-09-03 against
revision 1.12.0:

| clause | state | why |
|---|---|---|
| `R10-local-by-default` | **pass** | local embedder, active |
| `R10-no-egress` | **FAIL** | gap A below |
| `R15-residue-inventory` | **pass** | 0 residue outside 1 declared root |
| `R15-model-cache-under-declared-roots` | **pass** | upstream PR #27's doing |
| `R15-uninstall-removes-declared-state` | not-offered | gap B below |
| `R22-pause-stops-background-work` | not-run | gap C below |
| `R22-pause-holds-across-restart` | not-run | gap C below |

Three of seven green. The rung is a conjunction, so that is not partial credit.

## The gaps, each with the sentence that establishes it

**Gap A — the default configuration phones home (R10).** `ZOTEUS_UPDATE_CHECK`
defaults to true in the reviewed build (`fork/dist/config.js`), and the server
logged "Update available: Zoteus 1.13.0 (running 1.12.0)" during the run. R10:
*"Without an explicit opt-in, my library text and my queries MUST NOT leave this
machine"*, with the one-time model-weight download named as the sole exception.
Caught only by the DNS detector — the off-machine count was 0, because inside a
no-route namespace a hostname attempt dies at resolution and leaves no connect
at all. **Not yet established:** whether the update check accounts for all four
lookups. One arm settles it — the same assertion with `ZOTEUS_UPDATE_CHECK=false`
— and it belongs beside the existing net-shared control, never as a graded
configuration.

**Gap B — nothing published says how to remove it (R15).** *Restated
2026-09-03 after a ruling; the earlier reading, that zoteus must grow a callable
uninstall verb, is retired — see the log.* R15's body requires that "the target's
real uninstall surface removes them" and that a residue inventory check the
declaration is complete. For an external MCP server with no host uninstall
lifecycle to hook, that surface is a **published removal procedure**, and the
ruling of 2026-09-03 lets the harness execute one verbatim and sweep. So what is
missing is not a verb: it is documentation, and its absence is what makes the
clause ungradeable.

Upstream PR #27 (merged 2026-08-29) is what makes a correct procedure *writable*
at all, by pinning the model cache under the data directory — before it, "delete
the data directory" would have been wrong, which is exactly the failure the sweep
exists to catch. §5.2.7's maintenance purge is not a candidate for this role and
never was: it is checkpoint plus VACUUM plus compaction, which keeps a living
index rather than removing one.

**Gap C — R22's restart clause has no path to green through the current
assertions, and one of the two reasons this ticket gave for that is retired.**
*Restated 2026-09-04 after source verification against the reviewed baseline
(b0e0bc8/v1.13.0); the earlier reading is preserved in the log rather than
silently corrected.* The adapter's three claims about `stop`/`build` — the
cancel flag is in-memory, the checkpoint reaches disk regardless, and nothing
auto-resumes — are now confirmed by reading `index-manager.ts`/`build.ts`/
`sqlite-index.ts` directly rather than taken from the adapter's own argument.
`ZOTEUS_INDEX_AUTO_REFRESH`, the variable this ticket previously named as the
reason the restart clause's falsifying arm was disabled, does not exist
anywhere in the reviewed source (`config.ts`'s ~50-key env schema has no such
key, and it is silently ignored by design, like every unknown `ZOTEUS_*`
variable) — so that arm was never actually neutered by it, on this baseline.
What genuinely blocks both clauses is worse than "no work counters exist"
(ticket 0033): `check_pause_stops_background_work` and
`check_pause_holds_across_restart` (`bench/acceptance/assertions.py`) each
gate on the counters *and* on the harness's only wired perturbation,
`EDIT_ONE_ITEM`, which zoteus's adapter refuses on a principled R15 ground
(a write to the user's own library) that 0033's ledger work does not touch.
0033 shipping counters alone would not unblock gap C. See the log for the full
derivation, file:line evidence, and a concrete (unimplemented) sketch of an
R22-only check that sidesteps both: a new adapter-mediated perturbation
("resume embedding a seeded, incompletely-embedded index" via `action:build`)
and a direct read of the sqlite index file's own passage/vector counts and
`checkpoint` meta row — the same technique the adapter already uses for the
schema-version check — rather than the `work.<stage>.<trigger>.<outcome>`
vocabulary, which gap C's own perturbation needs no trigger classification
from. Filed as child ticket 0636, deliberately independent of 0033/0032.

## Actions

1. Settle gap C's measurement. Re-derived 2026-09-04: not resolvable through
   the current assertions regardless of 0033; needs 0636 (a new R22-only check)
   or a change to the shared goal-2 perturbation vocabulary.
2. Run gap A's discriminating arm and attribute the four lookups.
3. Decide the upstream form of gaps A and B against `GOVERNANCE.md` and
   `SYNC.md`'s measured asymmetry, and file.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] all seven goal-1 clauses green for zoteus, each resting on a run
- [ ] no clause green by waiver, and none green where its falsifying arm was
      disabled in the run that passed it

## Why one tracker per rung, per target

The ladder's rungs are conjunctions: a rung is kept when every one of its members
holds, and at no state before that. Nothing in the repository asserted that
conjunction *for a named target* — `README.md` reports each requirement's
standing across the project, and `bench/results/0604-ladder-matrix/MATRIX.md`
reports each clause against each target, but neither answers "is this rung kept
for zoteus". These three trackers answer exactly that, one each, and they close
only when their rung's every clause is green for zoteus.

zoteus is the named target because *works for me* is the acceptance standard and
this is the tool the author runs. A green here is a green for zoteus and for
nothing else; the other four roster targets are measured by the same layer and
are not this tracker's business.

## Children

Children are filed when their work starts, not up front. The gaps below are
enumerated with the requirement sentence each rests on, which is what a child
ticket would carry anyway; filing four stubs today would inflate the queue
without advancing anything (severity floor, `rules/workflow.md`). This tracker is
edited to list each child as it is created.

| child | scope | state |
|---|---|---|
| 0629 | gap A — attribute the four network lookups under `ZOTEUS_UPDATE_CHECK=false` | filed 2026-09-03, findings complete; confirming arm still not-run (structural reason, tracked by 0633) |
| 0630 | gap B — draft `UNINSTALL.md` as the R15 removal procedure | filed 2026-09-03 |
| 0633 | not a gap-A/B/C child — a harness finding surfaced while running 0629's confirming arm: account posture cannot compose with the podman-unshare sandbox fallback | filed 2026-09-04, open |
| 0634 | gap A's Action 3 (issue-drafting half) — draft the upstream issue for the default-on update check | filed 2026-09-04, draft complete at `verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0634.md`, staged not sent |
| 0636 | gap C — an R22-only check via a new perturbation and a direct sqlite read, independent of 0033/0032 | filed 2026-09-04 |
